{"name":"Morbid Princess","hex":"#9e0e64","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"morbid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or afflicted by disease. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Taking an interest in, or fixating on, unhealthy or unwholesome subjects such as death, decay, disease."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morbid"},{"term":"princess","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female member of a royal family other than a queen, especially a daughter or granddaughter of a monarch. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A woman or girl who excels in a given field or class."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/princess"}],"entries":[{"title":"Disease","blocks":[{"text":"A disease is a particular abnormal condition that adversely affects the structure or function of all or part of an organism and is not immediately due to any external injury. Diseases are often known to be medical conditions that are associated with specific signs and symptoms. A disease may be caused by external factors such as pathogens or by internal dysfunctions. For example, internal dysfunctions of the immune system can produce a variety of different diseases, including various forms of immunodeficiency, hypersensitivity, allergies, and autoimmune disorders."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Michael_Ancher%2C_Den_syge_pige%2C_1882%2C_KMS4002%2C_Statens_Museum_for_Kunst.jpg/330px-Michael_Ancher%2C_Den_syge_pige%2C_1882%2C_KMS4002%2C_Statens_Museum_for_Kunst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disease"},{"title":"Princess","blocks":[{"text":"Princess is a title used by a female member of a regnant monarch's family or by a female ruler of a principality. The male equivalent is a prince. Most often, the term has been used for the consort of a prince, or for the daughter of a monarch. A crown princess can be the heir apparent to the throne or the spouse of the heir apparent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg/330px-Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Poison_ivy_rash.JPG/500px-Poison_ivy_rash.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Poison_ivy_rash.JPG/1280px-Poison_ivy_rash.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Poison_ivy_rash.JPG/500px-Poison_ivy_rash.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This rash only affects one part of the body, so it is a localized disease.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APoison_ivy_rash.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Walking_the_dog_7th_Brigade_Park_Chermside_P1040698.jpg/500px-Walking_the_dog_7th_Brigade_Park_Chermside_P1040698.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Walking_the_dog_7th_Brigade_Park_Chermside_P1040698.jpg/1280px-Walking_the_dog_7th_Brigade_Park_Chermside_P1040698.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Walking_the_dog_7th_Brigade_Park_Chermside_P1040698.jpg/500px-Walking_the_dog_7th_Brigade_Park_Chermside_P1040698.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Regular physical activity, such as riding a bicycle or walking, reduces the risk of lifestyle diseases.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWalking_the_dog_7th_Br